WEBVTT

00:02:59.172 --> 00:03:01.117
if you only lived for a day.

00:03:01.141 --> 00:03:05.522
So like if human life span was only a day,
and we lived in winter,

00:03:05.546 --> 00:03:07.171
then you would go your entire life

00:03:07.195 --> 00:03:09.768
without ever seeing a tree
with a leaf on it.

00:03:09.792 --> 00:03:11.847
And there would be so many
human generations

00:03:11.871 --> 00:03:13.895
that would pass by within a single winter

00:03:13.919 --> 00:03:16.315
that you may not even have access
to a history book

00:03:16.339 --> 00:03:20.141
that says anything other than the fact
that trees are always lifeless sticks

00:03:20.165 --> 00:03:21.696
that don't do anything.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.379
Of course, this is ridiculous.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.553
We know that trees
are just waiting for summer

00:03:25.577 --> 00:03:26.926
so they can reactivate.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.125
But if the human life span

00:03:29.149 --> 00:03:32.228
were significantly shorter
than that of trees,